Salary - Circa £55,000 - Salary is dependent on experience and will be assessed in line with the candidate's skills, knowledge and relevant expertise.

&nbsp;

The Role…

As our QA Engineer, you’ll play a key role in making sure Hearst’s websites and apps deliver a seamless, reliable experience for millions of users across the UK. Working closely with Product, Design, Engineering and Editorial teams, you’ll test new features, challenge how things work, uncover issues and help bring great digital experiences to life.

You’ll work across our global platforms, making sure new developments are not only technically robust, but work brilliantly for our UK audiences. From new product launches to everyday improvements, you’ll help set the standard for quality at every stage of the journey.

Main Duties…

• Plan and carry out testing for website and app features across different devices, browsers and operating systems.

• Check that changes meet agreed requirements and work well for people using our products.

• Report bugs clearly, including steps to reproduce them, and work with engineers to confirm fixes.

• Run regression tests to check that new releases have not affected existing features.

• Contribute to test plans and release checks throughout the development process.

• Work with engineering teams on optimising automated testing by identifying suitable test cases.&nbsp;

• Use AI enabled testing tools and workflows to help identify risks, improve test coverage and make quality checks more efficient.

